Theorem L-1: Lattice join commutativity

  Preconditions:
    - a, b are AimsState elements per the canonical proof notation
      sec-Per-Dimension-Symbol-Set
    - join is the product-lattice componentwise join per Annex E §AIMS + L-1 (commutativity claim)

  Soundness property:
    Forall a, b in AimsState. join(a, b) = join(b, a)

  Proof obligation:
    Componentwise: for each dimension d, dim_join_d(a_d, b_d) =
    dim_join_d(b_d, a_d).

    Per-dimension proof:
      Access (Borrowed < Owned, height 1):
        max-based on totally ordered carrier; max commutative.
      Consumption (Dead < Linear < Affine < Unrestricted, height 3):
        max-based on totally ordered carrier; max commutative.
      Cardinality (Absent < Once < Many, height 2):
        max-based on totally ordered carrier; max commutative.
      Uniqueness (Unique < MaybeShared < Shared, height 2):
        max-based on totally ordered carrier; max commutative.
      Locality (BlockLocal < FunctionLocal < ArgEscaping < HeapEscaping
                < Unknown, height 4):
        max-based on totally ordered carrier; max commutative.
      Shape (flat lattice: equal stays; unequal -> NonReusable):
        case analysis (a_d == b_d -> a_d; a_d != b_d -> NonReusable);
        symmetric in a_d, b_d; commutative.
      Effect (3-bit flag set, componentwise OR):
        OR commutative on each Bool flag.

    All dimensions commutative implies product commutative.
    Lattice canonicalization (L-7 idempotence + L-8 join-preservation)
    preserves the equality across the canonicalize wrapper.

